title Mycelium Voucher r2 — the proof of position travels, and the signature survives the wire
prompt baton prin recur — continue the Voucher journey Lindy-first crux-first, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think r1 landed and sent (voucher.rye, both remotes, HEAD 72bf81f896). The loop recurs, so I took the next rung — r2, travel — mirroring statement_bron/lapse_bron: a proof a holder cannot hand to another is only a local reading, so it must cross as readable bytes.
think Read statement_bron.rye in full to mirror its shape: to_hex/from_hex/nibble helpers, a bounded token splitter, a purpose-built reader refusing UnknownField (never dropped), and the r2 crux carried as the record's OWN law (statement_bron carries reconciliation; the Voucher carries its signature). Designed format voucher-v1 as five lines — node · head · account · position(3 ints) · sig — the widest line (position) being four tokens, so the splitter is [4].
think Wrote voucher_bron.rye: render lays the five lines; parse tracks have_node/head/account/position/sig, requires all five (BadFormat on a missing field), and — the crux — runs voucher.verify_voucher(out) after reading, refusing BadSignature if the recovered slip does not verify over its bound facts. Caught two bugs before building: a method-call shim (out.verify_voucher() would resolve against the Voucher type's namespace, not this file's free fn) rewritten to voucher.verify_voucher(out); and an over-engineered bad-header refusal (a no-op self-assignment splice) replaced with a clean static "format voucher-v2\n" (the header check returns before any field is read).
obs GREEN on the first build after those fixes. The open-pledge voucher (balance 0 · reserved 100 · received 100) renders and parses back byte-for-byte (fixed point re-render diffed equal); the recovered voucher verifies offline AND still passes r1's check_against the very Dag it vouches; a tampered position (balance +1) re-rendered breaks the signature and refuses BadSignature; bad header · unknown field · bad hex · missing field each refuse their named error.
obs Additive discipline held: composed voucher public API only (make_voucher · verify_voucher · check_against · the Voucher fields · pk_len · order_head_len), edited no module, the Voucher r1 re-runs GREEN at the witness door. TAME style check clean (voucher_bron not flagged), width-check exit 0. Demo node/keeper seeds — no key/funds/network/custody.
loom witness=mycelium_voucher_bron_witness record_lines=5 refusals=5 first_build_after_fixes=green
file mycelium/voucher_bron.rye r2 — render/parse a format voucher-v1 record, the signature carried as the record's own law (BadSignature on a mangled slip)
file tools/mycelium_voucher_bron_witness.rish the r2 witness — selftest GREEN + fixed-point/verify/tamper assertions + the Voucher r1 re-run at the door
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md folded the Voucher r2 landing beside r1; git nib refreshed to living HEAD in the same work commit
recommend keep-going Voucher r3 (the attestation reads across a Knot — a node vouches a position over a ledger resolved across an epoch cut, the order-head folding the whole agreed order base included), then r4 true to the bytes (app == awk over a real fixture, order-head recomputed matches the signed one). A served voucher · per-account mint authority · breach renames (cairn-first) · deep debride · seed force-push stay the maintainer's hand.
